We have the equation $\frac{3+x}{5+x}=\frac{1+x}{2+x}$.
Simplifying, we get \begin{align*}
(3+x)(2+x)&=(5+x)(1+x)\\
6+5x+x^2&=5+6x+x^2\\
x&=\boxed{1}.
\end{align*}

